## Rule Organization

### Directory Structure
```
.cursor/
├── rules/
│   ├── base/              # Core functionality rules
│   ├── departments/       # Department-specific rules
│   ├── features/         # Feature-specific rules
│   ├── meta/            # Meta rules for management
│   ├── validation/      # Validation and testing rules
│   └── prompt-templates/ # Reusable prompt templates
```

### File Naming Conventions
- Use kebab-case for file names
- Include category prefix when appropriate
- Use descriptive names that indicate purpose
- Always use .mdc extension
- Follow pattern: `[category]-[description].mdc`

### Rule Categories
- Base Rules: Core functionality and standards
- Department Rules: Department-specific guidelines
- Feature Rules: Feature-specific implementations
- Meta Rules: Rule management and organization
- Validation Rules: Testing and verification
- Templates: Reusable prompt patterns

## Rule Structure

### YAML Frontmatter
```yaml
---
description: Clear description of rule purpose
globs: ["*.php", "*.js"]  # File patterns
alwaysApply: true/false   # Always apply rule
priority: low/medium/high/critical
---
```

